# Binaries live in git-lfs. Keep this list in sync with EXTS in
# scripts/lfs-normalize.sh and BINARY_EXTS in scripts/repo-audit.sh;
# scripts/repo-audit.sh fails when a committed binary type is missing.
#
# The character classes are not decoration. Git matches attribute patterns
# case-sensitively on Linux, so a camera's IMG_1234.JPG slips past a plain
# *.jpg, gets checked out as a raw pointer in CI, and ships to the server as a
# 131-byte text file. macOS hides this: its filesystem is case-insensitive, so
# the pattern matches locally and the bug only ever appears in the deploy.
# See docs/lfs-cleanup.md.
*.[pP][nN][gG] filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[jJ][pP][gG] filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[jJ][pP][eE][gG] filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[gG][iI][fF] filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[wW][eE][bB][pP] filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[aA][vV][iI][fF] filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[pP][dD][fF] filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[pP][sS][dD] filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[mM][pP]4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[mM][oO][vV] filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.[zZ][iI][pP] filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
